  "presentation_summary": [
    "55-year-old man with HIV, hepatitis C, hypertension, uncertain TB status, smoking history, and remote heroin/cocaine use presented with 2 weeks of gradually worsening pleuritic chest pain.",
    "He had productive cough with cupful yellow foul-smelling sputum, dyspnea on exertion, and chills, but denied fever and headache.",
    "He was afebrile with room-air oxygen saturation 96%; exam showed decreased bilateral breath sounds, bibasilar crackles, dullness to percussion in the left lower lobe, and 1+ lower-extremity edema.",
    "Presentation labs showed WBC 10.2 x10^9/L, neutrophils 79.8%, platelets 39 x10^9/L, PT 19 seconds, and INR 1.6.",
    "Initial chest radiograph showed a left pleural effusion with an air-fluid level, and CT showed a loculated left pleural-space fluid collection with large gas volume and adjacent left lower-lung consolidation."
  ],
